Root readout was not measured against alternatives. Typed pooling, in which each node type is mean-pooled separately and concatenated onto the root, is the first ablation off this default and is listed as future work rather than claimed as tested.

Diagnostic gate

The gate comprises the three controls of \S\ref{sec:gate}, with all thresholds and their derivations declared before the run. The ablation margin is set at 0.02 C, the design's resolution limit; the degree-probe ceiling of 0.55 and the shuffle tolerance of 0.05 are both the top of the chance band at three standard errors of a C-index on ~1,360 held-out patients. The label shuffle runs under two permutation schemes, a global one which the gate judges and a within-Study one which is recorded but never gated on, since the latter destroys what the within-Study metric measures while preserving Study-level survival differences. Treatment counts for the degree probe are pulled outside every path a model loads from, because the frozen extract deliberately does not carry them. The relation-split probe of \S\ref{sec:relsplit} is reported separately and is deliberately not a fourth verdict, so that a follow-up cannot rewrite the verdict which prompted it; for the same reason its vocabulary of ATTRIBUTED, NOT ATTRIBUTED and REVERSED is kept distinct from PASS and FAIL.

Comparison statistics

All model differences are paired by fold. The reported 95% intervals assume an independence the folds do not have, since any two folds share about half of their training patients, and are therefore anti-conservative; no unbiased estimator of k-fold cross-validation variance exists \cite{bengio2004}. This caveat is attached to every recorded comparison as a data field rather than stated once.